{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082010Z_dev-03_staged_30b7", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "In Kim, Lee, Park and Shin (arXiv:1601.05089), the best fit for ψψ̄ → h2h2 (about 100%, via ψψ̄ → h2 → h2h2) used m_ψ = 69.2 GeV and m_h2 = 35.7 GeV. They gave ⟨σv⟩ = 2.26×10⁻²⁶ cm³ s⁻¹ with Ωh² = 0.121. The fit had χ² = 23.19 (p-value 0.39) with a J-factor rescaling of 𝒥 = 2.2. I did not read the paper's definition of 𝒥. I take it to be a multiplicative rescaling of the canonical J-factor.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "7"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 11.622, "tool_calls": 5, "tool_result_chars": 19124, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 863, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11901, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16127, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:20:22+00:00"}
